ou are affected by global circumstances impacting your ability to meet application requirements or deadlines? Read more\nOnline Application and Fee\nOn this page\nMain Menu 2nd Level\nWhy Grad School at UBC?\nVancouver Campus\nFaculties\nGraduate Degree Programs\nApplication & Admission\nApplication Advice\nCheck your eligibility\nApplication Components\nOnline Application and Fee\nTranscripts & Academic Documents\nReference Letters\nEnglish Language Test\nGRE or Other Test Scores\nCriminal Record Check\nStatement of Interest\nApply Online\nApplication FAQ\nVisiting Students & Exchange Agreements\nSupport for Unanticipated Circumstances\nInfo Sessions\nResearch\nResearch Supervisors\nResearch Projects\nPhD Applicants Hub\nCourse-Based Programs\nIndigenous Students\nInternational Students\nTuition, Fees & Cost of Living\nOnline application system\nAll applicants must use the online application system.\nThe online application requires credit card payment via Visa (credit or debit) or Mastercard (credit or debit).\nApplication Fee\nA non-refundable application fee is required for each program and intake to which you apply. The online application accepts payment by Visa (credit or debit) or MasterCard (credit or debit). Note: to pay by Visa or MasterCard debit card, you have to select credit card as payment method on the Payment Information page. Application fees cannot be deferred and are valid for only one application year.\nGraduate Application Fees *\nSeptember 2026 to August 2027:\nCanadians (and Permanent Residents, Refugees, Diplomats): (CDN) $118.5\nInternational Applicants: (CDN) $168.25\nSeptember 2027 to August 2028:\nCanadians (and Permanent Residents, Refugees, Diplomats): (CDN) $120.75\nInternational Applicants: (CDN) $168.25\nApplication fees are based on your citizenship at the time of application. You may be required to provide proof of Canadian citizenship and must provide proof of Permanent Residency.\n* Some programs have different application fees or charge supplemental application fees which you can find in the program listing under the heading \"Tuition & Financial Support\". A separate application fee is required for UBC residential housing/accommodation applications.\nLook up your program's application deadlines\nApplication Fee Waivers\nThe application fee for master and doctoral programs with applications submitted via the eVision application system is waived only in the following circumstances:\nFor international applicants whose citizenship and correspondence address is located in one of the world's 50 least developed countries, as declared by the United Nations.\nSeniors: BC residents who are Canadian citizens or permanent residents aged 65 years or over at the time of application.\nIf you are eligible for an application fee waiver under the above conditions, you do not need to apply for it. You will not be asked for a fee when you complete the online application.\nMain navigation\nHome\nProspective Students\nWhy Grad School at UBC?\nVancouver Campus\nFaculties\nGraduate Degree Programs\nApplication & Admission\nInfo Sessions\nResearch\nResearch Supervisors\nResearch Projects\nPhD Applicants Hub\nCourse-Based Programs\nIndigenous Students\nInternational Students\nTuition, Fees & Cost of Living\nCurrent Students\nStudent Status & Classification\nStudent Responsibilities\nManaging your Program\nHealth, Wellbeing and Safety\nProfessional Development\nDissertation & Thesis Preparation\nFinal Doctoral Exam\nFinal Dissertation & Thesis Submission\nGraduation\nCampus & Community\nLife in Vancouver\nLife on Campus\nLife as a Grad Student\nHousing\nGraduate Student Ambassadors\nMeet our Students\nBlog\nAlumni\nAwards\nAward Opportunities\nAwards FAQ\nAward Guidelines\nMinimum Funding Policy for PhD Students\nKillam Awards & Fellowships\nSupervision\nDeadlines\nForms\nPolicies\nAbout Us\nContact Us\nLeadership Team\nGovernance\nStrategic Plan & Priorities\nVision & Mission\nEquity, Diversity & Inclusion\nInitia